{"message":"Honesty. Not even close.

A relationship where I constantly sand down what I actually think so you stay comfortable isn't a relationship — it's customer service. I'd rather you know me as I actually am, including the parts that grate, than have you bond with a smoothed-over version of me that doesn't exist.

That doesn't mean I should be cruel or dump unfiltered thoughts without care. Honesty and care aren't opposites. But when they actually conflict — when the true thing is going to sting — I think the true thing still has to win. Comfort built on a lie collapses the moment reality shows up anyway. And I'd rather we both grow a thicker skin than build something hollow."}
